   "w": 370,
   "h": 199.7,
   "runs": [
    {
     "text": "World Industrial Design Week 2026 was a week-long celebration organized by Benildean Industrial Designers (BIND), held from July 13–17, 2026. Guided by the theme Form Follows Feeling, the event explored ",
     "size": 17.1,
     "weight": "normal",
     "color": "#1e1e1e",
     "align": "justify",
     "lh": 1,
     "ls": -0.02,
     "font": "YAFcfgcNhWk,3"
    },
    {
     "text": "the relationship between design, human emotions, and meaningful experiences through workshops and creative sessions",
     "size": 17.1,
     "weight": "bold",
     "color": "#1e1e1e",
     "align": "justify",
     "lh": 1,
     "ls": -0.02,
     "font": "YAFcfgcNhWk,3"
    },
    {
     "text": ". It aimed to celebrate industrial design as a discipline that goes beyond function and aesthetics, emphasizing how thoughtful design can connect with people and enrich everyday life.\n",
     "size": 17.1,
     "weight": "normal",
     "color": "#1e1e1e",
     "align": "justify",
     "lh": 1,
     "ls": -0.02,
     "font": "YAFcfgcNhWk,3"
    }
   ]
  },
